AUTO MODE ADDED 2026-08-22 (user request: since Deinterlace has to be
manually configured per file even though it's remembered once set, add
an "Auto" choice to Preferences > General > Video "Deinterlace by
default" that detects whether a frame needs deinterlacing on its own,
without any media-info scanning of Vivace's own). Investigated first
whether this needed any new detection code at all -- it doesn't: yadif
and bwdif already have a built-in "deint" AVOption (verified against
FFmpeg's real n7.1 yadif.h: YADIF_DEINT_ALL=0, YADIF_DEINT_INTERLACED=1)
that, when set to "interlaced" instead of "all", deinterlaces only
frames the DECODER ITSELF flagged AV_FRAME_FLAG_INTERLACED -- a real,
per-frame, decoder-authoritative flag FFmpeg derives directly from the
bitstream's own coding structure (e.g. MPEG-2's picture_structure or
H.264's field_pic_flag/SEI), passing every other frame through
untouched. So "Auto" needed no scanning logic of Vivace's own at all --
only choosing "interlaced" over "all" for this one mode, on top of the
filter-graph machinery this patch already has.

Confirmed via a direct code read that the pre-existing hardcoded
deint=0 does NOT mean deinterlacing is always active: it only takes
effect once the DEINTERLACE MODE ITSELF is turned on (VIVACE_DEINTERLACE_
MODE > 0 in VideoRenderer::renderInternal()) -- mode 0 (None, the
default) bypasses the whole Deinterlacer construction/avfilter-graph
path entirely, so nothing was ever deinterlaced unconditionally
regardless of user settings.

SMPlayer's own Deinterlace enum (mediasettings.h: NoDeinterlace, L5,
Yadif, LB, Yadif_1, Kerndeint) has no "Auto" equivalent, confirming there
is nothing to port from the reference implementation here -- this is a
genuinely new capability beyond what SMPlayer/mplayer/mpv offer.

Design: `Deinterlacer::Mode` gained `Auto = 3`. Auto always selects the
bwdif filter (the higher-quality of the two supported filters, per this
patch's own earlier reasoning above) -- `ensureGraph()`'s filter-name
selection changed from `m_mode == Bwdif ? "bwdif" : "yadif"` to
`m_mode == Yadif ? "yadif" : "bwdif"`, so both Bwdif (2) and Auto (3)
resolve to "bwdif". The avfilter args string is now built conditionally:
`"mode=0:parity=-1:deint=1"` for Auto, `"mode=0:parity=-1:deint=0"`
(unchanged) for explicit Yadif/Bwdif. VideoRenderer::renderInternal()'s
one-time diagnostic qWarning() was updated to report "bwdif,
auto/interlaced-only" for mode 3 instead of misreporting it as plain
Yadif.

